#import "/_lib/0.1.1.typ": *
#show: template

#taxon[Idea]
// #title[Title]

A #local("00DT")[species] is a function from the #local("00DD")[type of finite sets] $"FinSet"$ to the type of sets $"Set"$. Using the #local("008Q")[axiom of univalence] we show that $"FinSet"$ splits into connected components, indexed by the natural numbers such that the $n$-th connected component is precisely the classifying type of the symmetric group in $n$ letters $Sigma_n$.
In that spirit any species $F$ is given by a family of group actions $F_n : Sigma_n -> "Set"$, allowing us to think about species using #local("00FX")[Univalent Group Theory]
